  "description": "The 2026 general election for Pennsylvania's 10th Congressional District features a rematch between incumbent Republican Rep. Scott Perry and Democratic challenger Janelle Stelson. Perry defeated Stelson by just 5,133 votes (50.6% to 49.4%) in 2024, making this one of the most competitive House races in the country. The district, which includes all of Dauphin County and parts of Cumberland and York Counties, is rated a 'toss-up' by the Cook Political Report. The race is seen as a key battleground in the fight for control of the U.S. House, with national Democrats targeting Perry as one of the most vulnerable Republican incumbents.",
